((date 2026-09-22) (slug top-of-funnel-capacity)
 (hypothesis
  "Top-N capacity at the screener: screening_config.max_buy_candidates 20 -> 40, nothing else changed (size, exposure, slots, grade floor untouched). Motivated by the 26y funnel (#2490: 36 % of monsters die at the top-N cut; ranking has no skill, so the cut at 20 is a lottery) and by the settled REJECTs on every breakout-gate width dial. Pre-registered (#2897, merged before any cell ran): realised AND Calmar better than the null at >= 2 of 3 salts -> ACCEPT(mechanism); if the arm-only cohort is >= 80 % losers at every salt -> REJECT as stale-entry breadth. d0 = the null s0 config with --emit-candidates as a funnel diagnostic + build tripwire.")
 (base_scenario
  "top-of-funnel-2026-09-21: t1-topn-40 = a0-pit-null + ((screening_config ((max_buy_candidates 40)))), paired per salt against the committed a0-pit-null-s{0,1,2}-v11 on _v11pit (9,364 entries, 27-entry yearly top-3000 PIT schedule 1999-2025), sweep-funnel @ad5a9e04e (main after #2882), SNAPSHOT_MAX_MMAP_HANDLES=12000, cells 4h48m / 4h16m / 3h59m. d0 tripwire: trades.csv md5 c1352be681e2eea3bf50d5c58a94f8a7 = committed null s0 (byte-identical metrics). V6 = 0 every cell, validator_diff -check V6 exit 0.")
 (window_id top3000-pit-1999-2025-record-26y-3salt) (baseline_label record-pit-null-v11pit)
 (variants
  (
   ((label topn-40-s0) (config_hash max-buy-candidates-40)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.3618) (mean_calmar 0.1056) (mean_return_pct 237.38) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 44.48)))))
   ((label topn-40-s1) (config_hash max-buy-candidates-40)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4089) (mean_calmar 0.1235) (mean_return_pct 303.97) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 43.84)))))
   ((label topn-40-s2) (config_hash max-buy-candidates-40)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4145) (mean_calmar 0.1266) (mean_return_pct 329.51) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 44.68)))))
  ))
 (verdict Accept)
 (notes
  "ACCEPT(mechanism) by the pre-registered rule: 2 of 3 salts clear both metrics (s0 237.4/0.106 vs 457.0/0.165 FAIL; s1 304.0/0.123 vs 188.0/0.077 CLEAR; s2 329.5/0.127 vs 152.0/0.069 CLEAR). NOT PROMOTABLE on this surface: one knob value (40), one window, one breadth tier - experiment-flag-discipline R3 + promotion-confirmation.md require the grid first ({30,40,60} x a disjoint 2019-2025 sub-window x a top-1000 schedule cell; promote only if the dispersion property holds in >= 2 of 3 cells). Default stays 20. LEVEL IS A SALT LOTTERY on both sides: cohort sizes identical at every salt (arm-only 280/280/265, null-only 241/298/261, ~36 % of each book) and the arm-only cohort's sign flips (-$0.87M / +$0.88M / +$0.85M vs null-only +$1.34M / +$0.004M / -$0.51M): s0 the null's draw holds the 2020+2025 monster cohorts, s1 the arm's holds ECHO (+$677k of +$0.88M), s2 the arm's holds six $230k+ winners across five years. Never quote +177pp or -220pp as the mechanism. ROBUST PROPERTY IS DISPERSION (n=3, PLAUSIBLE): arm realised 237-330 % (range 93pp) vs null 152-457 % (305pp); arm maxDD 43.8-44.7 (0.9pt) vs null 40.6-53.0 (12.4pt); means 290 vs 266 % and Calmar 0.119 vs 0.104; medians 304 vs 188 %. Three draws cannot separate 'less path-dependent' from 'the null's s0 is the outlier'. MECHANISM: the leak is SLOT POLICY, not screener capacity - d0 (funnel decomposition, results/d0-funnel-decomposition.md): the cap binds in 99.1 % of 1,335 weeks, cuts >= 20 names in 96.3 %, 33.8 A_plus names/week fall at it (admitted = 94 % A_plus, ranking = score then alphabetical), yet the book fills ~28 entries/yr into ~5 slots (concurrency 4.67-4.85 null vs 5.00-5.03 arm). Joining s0's arm-only entries to the null's own cascade (join.awk): 46 % were names the null ADMITTED the Friday before and never filled, 28 % were the marginal ranks 21-40, 25 % older resting orders. Widening re-draws which resting orders trigger first against the slots + cash floor; the marginal names are slightly worse (score 102-103 vs 106-107; winner rate 6.8/8.6/9.1 % vs 10.8/7.7/6.9 %, no robust sign). So #2490's '36 % of monsters die at top-N' is mostly a slot loss: screened, did not win the slot. FORWARD: next lever = slot-fill ordering when admitted > open slots (score, RS, volume ratio - never alphabetical; book spine item 7 supports RS for selection), pre-registered as a screener-ordering dial; not another cap-width point. RUNTIME: 4h48m/4h16m/3h59m at cap 12,000, peak RSS 6.45-6.47 GB; --emit-candidates doubled d0 (7h25m / 7.60 GB) - keep it off verdict cells. Artifacts: top-of-funnel-2026-09-21/results/t1-topn-40-s{0,1,2}-v11-* (+ per-salt reads), d0-* incl. both equity curves and the s0 join CSV, chain-A.log; README §Log + §Verdict."))
